diff --git a/crypto/sm2/README.md b/crypto/sm2/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..8a0ea1d2a5a0c4bc01d6358408bfc26e2d1b7a0b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crypto/sm2/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# SM2 extension
+
+This extension implements GB/T 32918.2 signatures and GB/T 32918.4 encryption
+on the named SM2 curve using the current BoringSSL EC and fixed-width scalar
+primitives. It is not a FIPS-approved algorithm. The ordinary ECDSA interfaces
+reject SM2 keys; the EVP key container remains `EVP_PKEY_EC`.
+
+## Reference and provenance
+
+The algorithms, identity binding, encoding and standard vectors were reviewed
+against Tongsuo 8.5.0, rather than importing its OpenSSL provider or build system:
+
+- `crypto/sm2/sm2_sign.c`: ZA, signature equations, scalar checks and the
+  fixed-width nonce / Montgomery arithmetic hardening.
+- `crypto/sm2/sm2_crypt.c`: SM3 counter KDF, zero-mask handling, C1/C3/C2 ASN.1
+  order and authentication.
+- `test/sm2_internal_test.c`: GB/T 32918.5-2016 Annex A and Annex C vectors,
+  serialized according to GM/T 0009-2012.
+
+Reference tag: <https://github.com/Tongsuo-Project/Tongsuo/tree/8.5.0>.
+The source ZIP SHA-256 is
+`35ec0ed648e799df8b5860d3716878812f117f6563607dcdf2709023b5e337f8`.
+The reviewed files match the ZIP, with SHA-256 values:
+
+| File | SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sm2_sign.c` | `aea2910562f42b2b5c20bf26a8037b8a835d879f4b76e26c43007b87aeb69780` |
+| `sm2_crypt.c` | `97d1d220ae9f39a80809645d933ad274c40576ce5ddc222eb08a14a6fb8a474b` |
+| `sm2_internal_test.c` | `0ae5dca5b3784e904fd2f5b138ea1e6b1092d654cb0c9817699e85191663adaa` |
+
+Tongsuo's referenced SM2 implementation credits the OpenSSL Project Authors and
+Ribose Inc., ported from Ribose contributions to Botan, under Apache License 2.0.
+The standard test vectors are reproduced with that attribution in `sm2_test.cc`.
+The implementation here is adapted to BoringSSL's current APIs and follows its
+Apache License 2.0 terms; see the repository `LICENSE`.
+
+## Deliberate integration differences
+
+- Only the standard SM2 curve and SM3 are supported. There are no arbitrary
+  curves, provider lookups or selectable SM2 hash algorithms.
+- ZA is `SM3(ENTL || ID || a || b || Gx || Gy || Px || Py)` with 32-byte field
+  elements. IDs are explicit, including an empty ID; null does not silently
+  substitute a default. The 16-bit bit-length permits at most 8191 ID bytes.
+  Generic EVP signing uses `1234567812345678`. RFC 8998 handshake signatures
+  must explicitly use `TLSv1.3+GM+Cipher+Suite` via the digest API.
+- Secret scalars use fixed-size `EC_SCALAR`, constant-time Montgomery arithmetic
+  and secret-point multiplication. Public verification uses the public-input
+  multiplication path. There is no secret-dependent `BN_div` or generic
+  `BN_mod_inverse`. Nonces are sampled from `[1,n-1]` with fresh BoringSSL RNG
+  output; signing also supplies a hash of the private scalar and digest as RNG
+  additional input. Retries are capped at 32 and a signing scalar of `n-1` is
+  rejected explicitly.
+- Ciphertexts use strict DER and reject trailing data, negative/out-of-range
+  coordinates, invalid curve points, malformed tags, empty plaintext and KDF
+  counter overflow. The size calculation uses checked `size_t` arithmetic.
+- Decryption authenticates C3 in a private buffer before copying plaintext to
+  the caller. A failed authentication leaves the output untouched. Ephemeral
+  scalars, shared coordinates, KDF state and temporary plaintext are cleansed.
+- Secret operations suppress FIPS indicators from internal RNG/EC helpers.
+  SM2 is not included in the approved-curve list.
+
+`sm2_test.cc` covers the published verification/decryption vectors, identity
+separation, randomized roundtrips, DER and authentication failures, scalar and
+buffer boundaries, ECDSA separation, EVP streaming semantics, key serialization
+and the SM2 certificate signature OID. These tests do not replace an independent
+cryptographic review or physical USBKey interoperability tests.
